# CODEOWNERS — example
#
# Rename to .github/CODEOWNERS and replace every placeholder before use.
# This file is what implements the peer-approval gate: with "Require review from
# Code Owners" enabled in branch protection, GitHub will not let a PR merge
# without an approval from an owner listed here.
#
# Syntax: <path pattern>  <owner> [<owner> ...]
# Owners are @username or @org/team-name. Teams must have write access to the
# repository or the rule is silently ignored.
# Last matching rule wins, so order matters — put the broad default first.

# ── Default owner for everything ────────────────────────────────────────────
*                           @ORG/REPLACE-ME-TEAM

# ── CI/CD and repository configuration ──────────────────────────────────────
# Workflow changes alter what runs with the repository's token. Restrict these
# to the people who own delivery and security.
/.github/                   @ORG/REPLACE-ME-PLATFORM-TEAM
/.github/workflows/         @ORG/REPLACE-ME-PLATFORM-TEAM
/.github/CODEOWNERS         @ORG/REPLACE-ME-PLATFORM-TEAM

# ── Security-relevant documents ─────────────────────────────────────────────
/SECURITY.md                @ORG/REPLACE-ME-SECURITY-TEAM

# ── Release metadata and its schema ─────────────────────────────────────────
# Records are append-only; the schema defines what an approval means.
/docs/schemas/              @ORG/REPLACE-ME-PLATFORM-TEAM
/releases/                  @ORG/REPLACE-ME-PLATFORM-TEAM

# ── AI review configuration ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
/.claude/                   @ORG/REPLACE-ME-PLATFORM-TEAM

# ── Documentation ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
/docs/                      @ORG/REPLACE-ME-TEAM

# ── Application code (CUSTOMIZE) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Add per-area owners once the source layout exists, most specific last. E.g.:
# /src/billing/             @ORG/REPLACE-ME-BILLING-TEAM
# /infra/                   @ORG/REPLACE-ME-PLATFORM-TEAM
